# The relay image builds from Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock, core/, relay/, the
# manifests of the other workspace members, and third_party/. Everything here
# is either the repository's own history or an artifact of another toolchain
# that the build context does not need.
# The NAS stack's secrets. Neither image reads them, but every build otherwise
# uploads them to the Docker daemon with the context.
.env
.env.*
.git
.github
target
.idea
.codex-remote-attachments
app/.dart_tool
app/build
app/.flutter-plugins*
app/web/pkg
app/android/.gradle
app/android/build
# Flutter's generated engine/plugin trees; hundreds of megabytes on a machine
# that has actually run a desktop or iOS build.
app/windows/flutter
app/ios/Pods
app/macos/Pods
app/linux/flutter/ephemeral
tools/web-smoke/node_modules
tools/web-bench/node_modules
tools/web-media/node_modules
# Native Flutter platform trees and host-only Dart tests/tools. Neither build
# uses them, and keeping them out means a change there does not invalidate the
# web build layer.
app/android
app/ios
app/macos
app/windows
app/linux
app/test
app/tool
